[38;2;106;159;181m  help: [0mProblem: v-for has higher priority than v-if, causing the entire list to iterate before filtering.
        Solution 1: Use a computed property:
          <script setup>
          const activeUsers = computed(() =>
          users.filter(u => u.isActive)
          )
          </script>
          <template>
          <li v-for="user in activeUsers" :key="user.id">
          </template>
        Solution 2: Wrap with <template>:
          <template v-for="user in users" :key="user.id">
          <li v-if="user.isActive">{{ user.name }}</li>
          </template>
        Reference: docs/content/rules/vue.md


